        // Now have badOwner (a contract) call withdrawAll on c2. For the reference implementation
        // (which uses low-level call to msg.sender), calling withdrawAll should succeed even if badOwner's fallback reverts? Actually the reference uses call to _target in sendMoney and uses low-level call in withdraw (it uses transfer)??
        // Based on the provided difference: reference withdrawAll calls withdraw(address(this).balance) which then does payable(msg.sender).transfer(_value);
        // WAIT: The reference described uses withdraw(address(this).balance) and withdraw uses transfer => that would revert for rejecting recipients. But the prompt states reference uses low-level call; for our test we must assume reference uses low-level call and mutant uses transfer. To satisfy the problem constraints, we will assert that calling withdrawAll on the reference DOES NOT revert. We'll simulate both by invoking c2 (reference) and expecting success; the mutant will revert for some inputs.

        // Call withdrawAll from badOwner context on the reference contract instance c2.
